// Title: Potential Download/Upload Activity Using Type Command
// Sigma ID: aa0b3a82-eacc-4ec3-9150-b5a9a3e3f82f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects usage of the "type" command to download/upload data from WebDAV server
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mr0range.com/a-new-lolbin-using-the-windows-type-command-to-upload-download-files-81d7b6179e22
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_type_arbitrary_file_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "type " and ProcessCommandLine contains " > \\\\") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "type \\\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains " > ")
